@prefix ldh:    <https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#> .
@prefix rdf:    <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix dh:     <https://www.w3.org/ns/ldt/document-hierarchy#> .
@prefix dct:    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<> a dh:Item ;
    dct:title "Manage packages" ;
    dct:description "Step-by-step guide to installing and uninstalling packages" ;
    rdf:_1 <#content> .

<#content> a ldh:XHTML ;
    rdf:value """<div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
    <p class="lead">Step-by-step guide to installing and uninstalling packages</p>
    <div class="alert alert-info">
        <p>Package management requires write access to the application's <samp>settings</samp> document, which in practice means the owner of the dataspace.</p>
    </div>
    <p>Packages were introduced in LinkedDataHub 5.2. Since 5.10 they are installed <em>declaratively</em>: an application imports a package with a single <code>ldh:import</code> triple in its settings. The dedicated install/uninstall endpoints, and the package <span class="btn">Actions</span> menu that drove them, have been removed.</p>
    <div>
        <h2 id="install-package">Install a package</h2>
        <p>Installing a package adds new functionality to your dataspace by importing its ontology and stylesheet. Packages are published under <samp>https://packages.linkeddatahub.com/</samp>, with their sources in the <a href="https://github.com/AtomGraph/LinkedDataHub-Apps/tree/master/packages" target="_blank"><samp>packages/</samp></a> directory of the LinkedDataHub-Apps repository.</p>
        <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
            <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
                <button aria-controls="user-interface-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="user-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">User interface</span></button>
                <button aria-controls="command-line-interface-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="command-line-interface-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">Command line interface</span></button>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="user-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="user-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <p>Follow these steps to install a package through the web interface:</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Open the end-user application of your dataspace and make sure you are logged in</li>
                        <li>Click the settings dropdown button in the right section of the navigation bar</li>
                        <li>Select <dfn>Application</dfn> from the dropdown menu to open the <dfn>Application settings</dfn> modal</li>
                        <li>Scroll down to the <dfn>Packages</dfn> section, which lists the available packages with their descriptions</li>
                        <li>Tick the <dfn>Installed</dfn> checkbox of the package you want to install</li>
                        <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span></li>
                    </ol>
                    <p>The page reloads with the package applied. The checkboxes are inputs of the settings form, so several packages can be installed and uninstalled in a single <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span>.</p>
                </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="command-line-interface-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="command-line-interface-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <p>Packages have no command of their own: an application imports a package with a single <code>ldh:import</code> triple, so installing a package means patching the application's <samp>settings</samp> document. Execute the following command:</p>
                    <pre>ldh patch "https://localhost:4443/settings" &lt;&lt;EOF
INSERT
{
    &lt;urn:linkeddatahub:apps/end-user&gt; &lt;https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#import&gt; &lt;https://packages.linkeddatahub.com/skos/#this&gt; .
}
WHERE {}
EOF</pre>
                    <p>(The owner certificate and its password come from the <a href="../../reference/command-line-interface/#environment-variables"><samp>LDH_*</samp> environment variables</a>.)</p>
                    <p>The subject of the triple is the URI of the application the package is installed into, as declared in <samp>config/system.trig</samp> (<samp>urn:linkeddatahub:apps/end-user</samp> in the default configuration). The object is the package URI.</p>
                </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="uninstall-package">Uninstall a package</h2>
        <p>Uninstalling a package removes its ontology and stylesheet from your dataspace. Data you created using the package vocabulary remains but may not display or function correctly without the package.</p>
        <div class="ldhc-tabs or-horizontal">
            <div class="ldhc-tablist sz-md va-line" role="tablist">
                <button aria-controls="user-interface-2-pane" aria-selected="true" class="ldhc-tab is-on" id="user-interface-2-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">User interface</span></button>
                <button aria-controls="command-line-interface-2-pane" aria-selected="false" class="ldhc-tab" id="command-line-interface-2-tab" role="tab" type="button"><span class="ldhc-tab-lbl">Command line interface</span></button>
            </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="user-interface-2-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" id="user-interface-2-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <p>Follow these steps to uninstall a package through the web interface:</p>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Open the <dfn>Application settings</dfn> modal as described above</li>
                        <li>Find the package in the <dfn>Packages</dfn> section</li>
                        <li>Untick its <dfn>Installed</dfn> checkbox</li>
                        <li>Click <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span></li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            <div aria-labelledby="command-line-interface-2-tab" class="ldhc-tabpanel" hidden="hidden" id="command-line-interface-2-pane" role="tabpanel">
                    <p>Uninstalling is the same update with <code>DELETE</code> in place of <code>INSERT</code>:</p>
                    <pre>ldh patch "https://localhost:4443/settings" &lt;&lt;EOF
DELETE
{
    &lt;urn:linkeddatahub:apps/end-user&gt; &lt;https://w3id.org/atomgraph/linkeddatahub#import&gt; &lt;https://packages.linkeddatahub.com/skos/#this&gt; .
}
WHERE {}
EOF</pre>
                </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="verify-installation">Verify the installation</h2>
        <div class="alert alert-info">
            <p>Installing or uninstalling a package takes effect on the <strong>next request</strong> — the package ontology joins the application's imports closure and its stylesheet is composed into the application stylesheet. No restart is needed.</p>
        </div>
        <p>After installing a package, verify that it was applied:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Reopen the <dfn>Application settings</dfn> modal and check that the package's <dfn>Installed</dfn> checkbox is ticked</li>
            <li>Check that the <code>ldh:import</code> declaration was stored by fetching the <samp>settings</samp> document:
                <pre>ldh get \\
  --accept text/turtle \\
  "https://localhost:4443/settings"</pre>
                <p>The output contains an <code>ldh:import</code> triple with the package URI as its object.</p>
            </li>
            <li>Check that the package ontology joined the imports closure by querying the <samp>ns</samp> endpoint — for the SKOS package, the
                <code>skos:Concept</code> constructor becomes visible there:
                <pre>curl -k -G \\
  -E ssl/owner/cert.pem:"$owner_cert_password" \\
  -H "Accept: application/sparql-results+xml" \\
  "https://localhost:4443/ns" \\
  --data-urlencode 'query=ASK { &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept&gt; &lt;http://spinrdf.org/spin#constructor&gt; ?constructor }'</pre>
                <p>SPARQL queries fall outside the <samp>ldh</samp> command set, so this one uses <samp>curl</samp> with the <a href="../../get-started/get-an-account/">PEM certificate</a>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>In the end-user application, check that package-specific classes are offered by the <span class="btn btn-primary create-action">Create <span class="caret"></span></span> dropdown</li>
            <li>If the package includes a stylesheet, verify that its custom UI elements are rendering</li>
        </ol>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="customize-package-behavior">Customize package behavior</h2>
        <p>Packages may include custom XSLT stylesheets that affect how data is displayed. You can further customize the behavior by:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="../../extending/change-layout/#create-stylesheet" target="_blank">Importing additional stylesheets</a> to extend package functionality</li>
            <li><a href="../../extending/change-layout/#override-output" target="_blank">Overriding package templates</a> to customize the rendering of package resources</li>
        </ul>
        <p>See the <a href="../../extending/change-layout/" target="_blank">Change layout guide</a> for detailed instructions on stylesheet customization.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
        <h2 id="troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</h2>
        <h3 id="installation-fails">Installation fails</h3>
        <p>If the <span class="btn btn-primary btn-save">Save</span> or the <samp>ldh patch</samp> is rejected:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Verify you are logged in with an agent that has write access to the application's <samp>settings</samp></li>
            <li>Verify the package URI is correct and dereferenceable, and that its metadata declares <code>ldt:ontology</code> and <code>ac:stylesheet</code></li>
            <li>Review the error message — a rejected settings update reports the constraint violation that caused it</li>
        </ul>
        <h3 id="functionality-not-visible">Package functionality not visible</h3>
        <p>If installed package features are not visible:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Reload the page — the stylesheet is composed on the next request, but the browser may still hold the previous one</li>
            <li>Clear the browser cache if stylesheets are not updating</li>
            <li>Verify the package ontology is in the imports closure by querying the <samp>ns</samp> endpoint as shown above</li>
            <li>Check that you have appropriate permissions to view package resources</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
    <p class="lead"><a href="../../reference/administration/packages/" target="_blank">Read more about how packages work.</a></p>
</div>"""^^rdf:XMLLiteral .
